# CI unit sync

When you change code under these paths, **update or add unit tests in the same change**, then run local preflight before considering the task done:

```bash
bash scripts/preflight_unit.sh
# or selective full mirror:
PREFLIGHT_ALL=1 bash scripts/preflight_unit.sh
```

## High-churn failure modes (already burned CI)

| Change | Update |
|--------|--------|
| `scenarios/**/system.md` | `tests/test_tools_core.py` (assert **stable section markers**, not ephemeral slogans) |
| `ToolExecutor` / approval sticky / state fields | `tests/test_tool_executor.py` mocks must include attrs the executor reads (`turn_id`, `run_id`, …) |
| `_resolve_pending` / checkpoint vs memory | `tests/test_turn_controller.py` must match intentional preference |
| contracts / OpenAPI / event schemas | `packages/contracts/tests` |

Do **not** claim “CI will catch it” — push is gated by `scripts/preflight_unit.sh` (git hook + Cursor push hook). Fix tests locally first.
